he previous choice or the first candidate in the list. Keeping a plan is valid when the evidence supports it; changing for appearances is not.\nWeigh robust development evidence against noisy local signals. High payment volume is not platform profit. Avoid outreach when its evidence is inadequate; do not search for a positive story or assert guaranteed profit. Select at least one actual observation ID, state the observed condition, and name a competing candidate you considered. These are concise public decision records, not private chain of thought. Explain in one short paragraph why the selected policy fits the CURRENT observations, including contrary evidence when material.",
